-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 2 -- THE SEAT.
--
-- SEAT: a person with a claim or a debt, or who has contracted, asking on facts they can state what the Act provides:
-- whether a contract must be in writing, whether interest runs, whether a claim survives death, whether a right can be
-- assigned, who contributes to a shared liability, what a family can claim after a wrongful death, whether a contract made
-- at 18 binds.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would
-- ask.  Nothing here is new law, and nothing here restates a rule: every question calls one layer-1 function.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact
-- the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure" (`My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and
--     a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A number the person may not know is asked as 0 and becomes NOTHING.
--   * The Minister's orders, the regulations that prescribe proceedings and requirements, and the public holidays are not among
--     the sources.  The questions take no list of public holidays.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on
-- these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a provision addresses only an official or the Minister (s 21(6), s 27(3) to (5), s 36(2)),
-- the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below, if at all.

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not a question.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

§ `The Civil Law Act 1909 -- my questions`

§§ `Courts and equity (ss 3 and 4)`

@export Must the court give me the equitable relief I claim in my civil case (s 3(a))?
GIVEN `my case is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case a civil cause or matter that you commenced in the court?
      `I claim an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim an equitable estate or right, or relief on an equitable ground, against a deed, instrument or contract or against a right, title or claim the defendant asserts (or relief founded on a legal right that before 1 January 1879 could only have been given on the equity side)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court give me the equitable relief I claim` IS
    `s 3(a) the court shall give the claimant the relief that the equity side ought to have given before 1 January 1879` `my case is a civil cause or matter commenced in the court` `I claim an equitable estate or right or relief on an equitable ground`

@export May a tenant for life or lives, or a leasehold tenant, commit voluntary waste on the land (s 4(3))?
GIVEN `the occupier is` IS A `Kind of tenant` @desc Is the occupier a tenant for life or lives, a leasehold tenant, or another kind of occupier?
      `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the estate or tenancy one without impeachment of waste?
      `there is a licence or other right to commit waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the occupier have a licence or other right to commit waste?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the tenant commit voluntary waste` IS
    `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `the occupier is` `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` `there is a licence or other right to commit waste`

@export Is a tenant who committed voluntary waste liable to me, the remainderman or reversioner, in damages (s 4(4))?
GIVEN `the tenant committed voluntary waste when the prohibition applied to the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the tenant commit voluntary waste at a time when the prohibition in section 4(3) applied to that tenant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the tenant liable to me in damages for voluntary waste` IS
    `s 4(4) the tenant is liable in damages to the remainderman or reversioner` `the tenant committed voluntary waste when the prohibition applied to the tenant`

@export May I, a mortgagor, sue for possession of the land or the rents and profits in my own name only (s 4(7))?
GIVEN `I am entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, the mortgagor, entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits of the immovable property?
      `the mortgagee has given notice of his intention to take possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the mortgagee given notice of his intention to take possession or to enter into the receipt of the rents and profits?
      `the claim arises on a lease or contract I made jointly with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim arise upon a lease or other contract that you made jointly with another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I sue for possession in my own name only` IS
    `s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` `I am entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits` `the mortgagee has given notice of his intention to take possession` `the claim arises on a lease or contract I made jointly with another person`

@export Is my assignment of a debt or other chose in action effectual in law to pass the legal right (s 4(8))?
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment absolute?
      `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment by writing under the hand of the person assigning?
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assignment purport to be by way of charge only?
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has express notice in writing been given to the debtor, trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my assignment of the debt effectual in law` IS
    `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor`

@export From what date does the legal right to the assigned debt pass to me (s 4(8))?
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment absolute?
      `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment by writing under the hand of the person assigning?
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assignment purport to be by way of charge only?
      `the date express notice in writing was given to the debtor` IS A DATE @desc On what date was express notice in writing given to the debtor?
      `express notice in writing has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has express notice in writing been given to the debtor?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what date does the legal right pass to me` IS
    `s 4(8) the date from which the legal right to the debt or chose in action passes` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `the date express notice in writing was given to the debtor` `express notice in writing has been given`

@export Has the legal right to the assigned debt passed to me by a given day (s 4(8))?
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment absolute?
      `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment by writing under the hand of the person assigning?
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assignment purport to be by way of charge only?
      `the date express notice in writing was given to the debtor` IS A DATE @desc On what date was express notice in writing given to the debtor?
      `express notice in writing has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has express notice in writing been given to the debtor?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask whether the right has passed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the legal right passed to me by a day` IS
    `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `the date express notice in writing was given to the debtor` `express notice in writing has been given` `the day asked about`

@export Can I, as assignee, give a good discharge for the assigned debt without the assignor joining in (s 4(8))?
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment absolute?
      `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assignment by writing under the hand of the person assigning?
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the assignment purport to be by way of charge only?
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has express notice in writing been given to the debtor, trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I give a good discharge for the debt` IS
    `s 4(8) the assignee has the power to give a good discharge for the debt or chose in action without the concurrence of the assignor` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is in writing under the assignor's hand` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor`

@export Is a stipulation as to time in my contract treated as of the essence only as equity would have treated it (s 4(9))?
GIVEN `before 23 July 1909 a court of equity would not have treated the stipulation as of the essence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a court of equity, before 23 July 1909, have declined to treat the stipulation as to time (or otherwise) as being or having become of the essence of the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is time of the essence of my contract` IS
    `s 4(9) the stipulation is construed and has effect as it would have had in equity` `before 23 July 1909 a court of equity would not have treated the stipulation as of the essence`

@export May the court grant me an interlocutory order for an injunction or appoint a receiver (s 4(10))?
GIVEN `it appears just or convenient that the order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court grant me an interlocutory injunction` IS
    `s 4(10) the court may grant a Mandatory Order or an injunction or appoint a receiver by an interlocutory order` `it appears just or convenient that the order should be made`

@export May the Singapore court grant interim relief in aid of my proceedings abroad (s 4(10A))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings in a civil or commercial matter?
      `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal, monetary or revenue law or measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings arise out of a fiscal, monetary or revenue law or measure?
      `the proceedings have been or are to be commenced outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the proceedings been, or are they to be, commenced outside Singapore?
      `it appears just or convenient that the order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court grant interim relief for my foreign proceedings` IS
    `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` `the proceedings are in a civil or commercial matter` `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal, monetary or revenue law or measure` `the proceedings have been or are to be commenced outside Singapore` `it appears just or convenient that the order should be made`


§§ `Gaming, wagering, maintenance and funding of claims (ss 5, 5A and 5B)`

@export Is my contract by way of gaming or wagering null and void (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `the contract is by way of gaming or wagering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract by way of gaming or wagering?
      `it is a subscription for a prize in a lawful game` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a subscription or contribution, or an agreement to subscribe or contribute, for or toward a plate, prize or sum of money to be awarded to the winner of a lawful game, sport, pastime or exercise (s 5(3))?
      `it is within the exceptions of section 5(3A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it within one of the exceptions in section 5(3A) (a contract with an exempted operator or organisation, a totalisator bet, a permitted private lottery, or a contract with a licensee under the Gambling Control Act 2022)?
      `it is saved by section 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it entered into by way of business and is its making or performance an investment activity (s 5(4))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my gaming or wagering contract null and void` IS
    `s 5(1) the contract by way of gaming or wagering is null and void` `the contract is by way of gaming or wagering` `it is a subscription for a prize in a lawful game` `it is within the exceptions of section 5(3A)` `it is saved by section 5(4)`

@export May I bring an action to recover a sum alleged to be won on a wager, or deposited with a stakeholder (s 5(2))?
GIVEN `the sum is alleged to be won upon a wager or deposited with a person to abide the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum of money or valuable thing alleged to be won upon a wager, or deposited in the hands of any person to abide the event on which a wager has been made?
      `it is within the exception of section 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract a subscription for a prize in a lawful game (s 5(3))?
      `it is within the exceptions of section 5(3A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract within one of the exceptions in section 5(3A)?
      `it is saved by section 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract saved by section 5(4) (made by way of business, an investment activity)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I sue to recover a sum won on a wager` IS
    `s 5(2) an action may be brought or maintained in the court for recovering the sum or thing` `the sum is alleged to be won upon a wager or deposited with a person to abide the event` `it is within the exception of section 5(3)` `it is within the exceptions of section 5(3A)` `it is saved by section 5(4)`

@export Is my bet on a totalisator within the exceptions to the nullity of wagers (s 5(3A)(c))?
GIVEN `the bet takes place on a totalisator run by or for the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club under an approved scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the bet take place on a totalisator conducted by or on behalf of the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club in accordance with an approved scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my totalisator bet within the exceptions` IS
    `s 5(3A)(c) the contract for betting on a totalisator is within the exception` `the bet takes place on a totalisator run by or for the Singapore Totalisator Board or a turf club under an approved scheme`

@export Is my promise to pay back a sum paid under a void wager, or to pay a commission in respect of it, null and void (s 5(6))?
GIVEN `the promise is to pay a sum paid under or in respect of a void gaming or wagering contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promise to pay a sum of money paid under or in respect of a contract rendered null and void by section 5(1) and (2)?
      `the promise is to pay a commission or fee in respect of such a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promise to pay a sum by way of commission, fee, reward or otherwise in respect of such a contract or of services connected with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my promise to repay a sum paid under a void wager null` IS
    `s 5(6) the promise express or implied is null and void` `the promise is to pay a sum paid under or in respect of a void gaming or wagering contract` `the promise is to pay a commission or fee in respect of such a contract`

@export Am I liable in tort merely because my conduct was maintenance or champerty (s 5A(1))?
GIVEN `the liability asserted rests only on the conduct being maintenance or champerty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability in tort that is asserted against you rest only on your conduct being maintenance or champerty as known to the common law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable in tort for maintenance or champerty` IS
    `s 5A(1) the person is liable in tort for the conduct on account of its being maintenance or champerty` `the liability asserted rests only on the conduct being maintenance or champerty`

@export Is my contract with a qualifying third-party funder contrary to public policy or illegal because it is maintenance or champerty (s 5B(2))?
GIVEN `a qualifying third-party funder provides funds for my costs in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a qualifying Third-Party Funder provide funds to a party for the purpose of funding all or part of that party's costs in the proceedings?
      `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings` IS A `My answer` @desc Are the proceedings prescribed dispute resolution proceedings (the class is set by regulations)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my third-party funding contract illegal as maintenance or champerty` IS
    `s 5B(2) the funding contract is contrary to public policy or otherwise illegal by reason that it is a contract for maintenance or champerty` `a qualifying third-party funder provides funds for my costs in the proceedings` (`what I say, as a fact` `the proceedings are prescribed dispute resolution proceedings`)

@export Does the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements for a third-party funding contract arise for me (s 5B(3))?
GIVEN `I am a qualifying third-party funder or the funded party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a qualifying Third-Party Funder or a funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I comply with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` IS
    `s 5B(3) the duty to comply with the prescribed requirements arises` `I am a qualifying third-party funder or the funded party`

@export Have I complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with (s 5B(3))?
GIVEN `I am a qualifying third-party funder or the funded party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a qualifying Third-Party Funder or a funded party in relation to a third-party funding contract?
      `I have complied and ensured that they are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I complied with the prescribed requirements for third-party funding` IS
    `s 5B(3) the person has complied with the prescribed requirements and ensured that they are complied with` `I am a qualifying third-party funder or the funded party` `I have complied and ensured that they are complied with`

@export May the third-party funder enforce its rights under the funding contract by action or arbitration (s 5B(4))?
GIVEN `the funder has ceased to be a qualifying third-party funder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Third-Party Funder ceased to be a qualifying Third-Party Funder?
      `the funder has failed to comply with a prescribed requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Third-Party Funder failed to comply with a prescribed requirement mentioned in section 5B(3)?
      `the right is connected with the disqualification or non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right one under or arising out of the funding contract affected by or connected with the disqualification or non-compliance?
      `relief against the disability has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has relief against the disability been granted under section 5B(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the funder enforce its rights under the funding contract` IS
    `s 5B(4) the right of the Third-Party Funder is enforceable by action or other legal proceedings including arbitration proceedings` `the funder has ceased to be a qualifying third-party funder` `the funder has failed to comply with a prescribed requirement` `the right is connected with the disqualification or non-compliance` `relief against the disability has been granted`


§§ `Contracts that must be in writing, trusts, the euro (ss 6 to 9)`

@export May I bring an action on this promise or agreement when there is no signed writing (s 6)?
GIVEN `the kind of action` IS A `Kind of action under section 6` @desc Is the action on an executor's special promise, a promise to answer for another's debt, an agreement made upon consideration of marriage, a contract for the sale of immovable property, an agreement not to be performed within a year, or another kind?
      `the promise or a memorandum of it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promise or agreement, or some memorandum or note of it, in writing?
      `it is signed by the party to be charged or his authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring an action on this promise without a signed writing` IS
    `s 6 an action may be brought on the promise or agreement` `the kind of action` `the promise or a memorandum of it is in writing` `it is signed by the party to be charged or his authorised person`

@export Is my action barred because there is no signed writing (s 6)?
GIVEN `the kind of action` IS A `Kind of action under section 6` @desc Is the action on an executor's special promise, a promise to answer for another's debt, an agreement made upon consideration of marriage, a contract for the sale of immovable property, an agreement not to be performed within a year, or another kind?
      `the promise or a memorandum of it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the promise or agreement, or some memorandum or note of it, in writing?
      `it is signed by the party to be charged or his authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it signed by the party to be charged or by some other person lawfully authorised by that party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my action barred for want of a signed writing` IS
    `s 6 the action is barred for want of a signed writing` `the kind of action` `the promise or a memorandum of it is in writing` `it is signed by the party to be charged or his authorised person`

@export Is my declaration of a trust of immovable property manifested and proved as section 7(1) requires?
GIVEN `the declaration respects immovable property or an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the declaration of trust respect immovable property or an interest in it?
      `it is manifested and proved by signed writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it manifested and proved by some writing signed by a person able to declare the trust?
      `it is made by his will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by his will?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my declaration of trust of immovable property properly proved` IS
    `s 7(1) the declaration of trust is manifested and proved as the subsection requires` `the declaration respects immovable property or an interest in it` `it is manifested and proved by signed writing` `it is made by his will`

@export Is the rule in Bain v Fothergill abolished in relation to my contract (s 8)?
GIVEN `the date my contract was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contract made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the rule in Bain v Fothergill abolished for my contract` IS
    `s 8 the rule in Bain v Fothergill is abolished in relation to the contract` `the date my contract was made`

@export May performance of my contract be made in this currency after the introduction of the euro (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `performance could, apart from the euro, be made in the currency originally designated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could performance, apart from the introduction of the euro, be made in the currency or currencies originally designated in the instrument?
      `the currency of performance` IS A `Currency of performance` @desc In which currency would performance be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `In what currency may performance be made after the euro` IS
    `s 9(2) performance may be made in the currency` `performance could, apart from the euro, be made in the currency originally designated` `the currency of performance`


§§ `Death, expectation of life, interest, charges, the husband (ss 10 to 14)`

@export Does a cause of action survive the death of the person it was against or vested in (s 10)?
GIVEN `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person when he died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the cause of action subsist against, or was it vested in, the person at the time of his death?
      `the kind of cause of action` IS A `Kind of cause of action` @desc Is it a claim for defamation, seduction, inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other, damages for adultery, breach of promise to marry, or another cause of action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my cause of action survive the death` IS
    `s 10 the cause of action survives the death of the person` `the cause of action subsisted against or was vested in the person when he died` `the kind of cause of action`

@export May the estate recover this head of damages where a cause of action survives for its benefit (s 10(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the cause of action survive for the benefit of the estate of the deceased person?
      `the head of damages` IS A `Head of damages for the benefit of an estate` @desc Are the damages exemplary damages, damages for loss of income after the death, or another head?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the estate recover this head of damages` IS
    `s 10(3)(a) the head of damages is recoverable for the benefit of the estate` `the cause of action survives for the benefit of the estate` `the head of damages`

@export In an action for personal injuries, can I recover damages for loss of expectation of life (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `the action is for damages for personal injuries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action an action for damages for personal injuries?
      `the damages are for loss of income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the damages in respect of loss of income?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I recover damages for loss of expectation of life` IS
    `s 11(1) damages are recoverable in respect of loss of expectation of life caused by the injuries` `the action is for damages for personal injuries` `the damages are for loss of income`

@export May the court order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the proceedings are tried in a court of record for a debt or damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings tried in a court of record for the recovery of a debt or damages?
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think fit to order interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court award me interest on my debt or damages` IS
    `s 12(1) the court may order interest to be included in the sum for which judgment is given` `the proceedings are tried in a court of record for a debt or damages` `the court thinks fit`

@export Can I create a charge or mortgage in favour of the person who owes me the debt, over my interest in it (s 13)?
GIVEN `the chose in action is enforceable by me against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the chose in action (for example a debt) enforceable by you against the person in whose favour you create the charge?
      `the charge or mortgage is over all or any of my interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the charge or mortgage over all or any of your interest in the chose in action?
      `it is created in favour of that other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it created in favour of that other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I charge my interest in a debt owed to me` IS
    `s 13 the first person is able to create the charge or mortgage over the chose in action` `the chose in action is enforceable by me against the other person` `the charge or mortgage is over all or any of my interest in it` `it is created in favour of that other person`

@export Is a husband liable merely because he is her husband for his wife's torts or for debts she incurred before the marriage (s 14(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the person is the husband of a married woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the husband of a married woman?
      `the liability is for her tort, or her contract, debt or obligation before the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability in respect of a tort committed by her (before or after the marriage) or a contract entered into, or debt or obligation incurred, by her before the marriage?
      `the liability arises by reason only of his being her husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability arise by reason only of his being her husband?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a husband liable for his wife's torts and earlier debts` IS
    `s 14(1)(a) the husband is liable in respect of the tort contract debt or obligation` `the person is the husband of a married woman` `the liability is for her tort, or her contract, debt or obligation before the marriage` `the liability arises by reason only of his being her husband`


§§ `Contribution between persons liable for the same damage (ss 15 to 19)`

@export May I recover contribution from another person who is liable in respect of the same damage (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `I am liable in respect of damage suffered by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable in respect of damage suffered by another person?
      `the other person is liable in respect of the same damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person liable in respect of the same damage, whether jointly with you or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I recover contribution from the other person liable for the same damage` IS
    `s 15(1) the person may recover contribution from the other person` `I am liable in respect of damage suffered by another person` `the other person is liable in respect of the same damage`

@export May I recover contribution after paying in bona fide settlement of a claim against me (s 15(4))?
GIVEN `I made or agreed to make a payment in bona fide settlement or compromise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made or agreed to make a payment in bona fide settlement or compromise of a claim made against you in respect of the damage (including a payment into court that has been accepted)?
      `I would have been liable if the factual basis of the claim could be established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been liable, assuming that the factual basis of the claim against you could be established?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I recover contribution after settling the claim` IS
    `s 15(4) the person is entitled to recover contribution in accordance with section 15 whether or not he was liable` `I made or agreed to make a payment in bona fide settlement or compromise` `I would have been liable if the factual basis of the claim could be established`

@export Where the claimant's damages were limited or reduced, what is the most I can be required to pay by way of contribution (s 16(3))?
GIVEN `the claimant could have recovered from me in an action brought in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the person who suffered the damage have brought an action in Singapore against you for it?
      `the damages were or would have been subject to a limit under a written law or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the damages subject to a limit imposed by or under a written law or by an agreement made before the damage occurred?
      `the damages were or would have been reduced for contributory negligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the damages subject to a reduction under section 3 of the Contributory Negligence and Personal Injuries Act 1953?
      `there was a corresponding foreign limit or reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a corresponding limit or reduction under the law of a country outside Singapore?
      `the contribution awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc What contribution has been awarded against you, in dollars?
      `the damages as limited or reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the claimant's damages as so limited or reduced, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much at most can I be required to pay by way of contribution` IS
    `s 16(3) the most the person is required to pay in respect of the damage by virtue of the contribution` `the claimant could have recovered from me in an action brought in Singapore` `the damages were or would have been subject to a limit under a written law or agreement` `the damages were or would have been reduced for contributory negligence` `there was a corresponding foreign limit or reduction` `the contribution awarded` `the damages as limited or reduced`

@export Am I entitled to costs in this action where more than one action was brought for the same damage (s 18)?
GIVEN `more than one action was brought for the damage against persons liable for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was more than one action brought in respect of the damage, by or for the person who suffered it, against persons liable in respect of it?
      `judgment was first given in this action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was judgment first given in this action?
      `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing this action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to costs when several actions were brought` IS
    `s 18 the claimant is entitled to costs in the action` `more than one action was brought for the damage against persons liable for it` `judgment was first given in this action` `the court is of the opinion that there was reasonable ground for bringing the action`

@export Do the sections on contribution affect a case where the debt or damage came before 1 January 1999 (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `the date the debt became due or the damage occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the debt become due or the damage occur?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the contribution sections apply to damage before 1 January 1999` IS
    `s 19(4) sections 15 to 18 affect the case` `the date the debt became due or the damage occurred`


§§ `Death caused by a wrongful act (ss 20 to 22)`

@export Is the person liable to an action for damages for a death caused by his wrongful act (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `death was caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was death caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default?
      `the injured person could have recovered damages had death not ensued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it such as would, had death not ensued, have entitled the person injured to maintain an action and recover damages?
      `the person is the one who would have been liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the one who would have been liable if death had not ensued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the wrongdoer liable to an action for a death` IS
    `s 20(1) the person is liable to an action for damages notwithstanding the death of the person injured` `death was caused by a wrongful act, neglect or default` `the injured person could have recovered damages had death not ensued` `the person is the one who would have been liable`

@export Am I a dependant of the deceased for a claim under section 20 (s 20(8) and (9))?
GIVEN `my relationship to the deceased` IS A `Relationship to the deceased` @desc Which of these describes your relationship to the deceased?
      `the basis of the relationship` IS A `Basis of the relationship` @desc On what basis is that relationship deduced (by blood, by adoption, by affinity, of the half blood, as a stepchild, as an illegitimate child)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a dependant of the deceased` IS
    `s 20(8) with (9) the person is a dependant of the deceased` `my relationship to the deceased` `the basis of the relationship`

-- The question takes no list of public holidays: a last day that is a Sunday moves to the next day (Interpretation Act s 50(b)), but a public holiday is not known.
@export Is my action under section 20 brought within 3 years after the death (s 20(5))?
GIVEN `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person die?
      `the date the action is brought` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my wrongful-death action brought in time` IS
    `s 20(5) the action is brought within 3 years after the death` `the date of the death` `the date the action is brought` EMPTY

@export May a claim for damages for bereavement be for my benefit (s 21(2))?
GIVEN `which of these describes me` IS A `Class of claimant for bereavement` @desc Are you the surviving wife or husband, a surviving child, a surviving parent (or the mother if the deceased was illegitimate), a person who treated the deceased minor as a child of the family, or a surviving brother or sister?
      `I survive the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you survive the deceased?
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a surviving spouse by or for whom a claim can be made?
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a surviving child by or for whom a claim can be made?
      `a claim can be made by or for a surviving parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a surviving parent by or for whom a claim can be made?
      `a claim can be made by or for a person who treated the deceased as a child of the family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a person who treated the deceased as a child of the family by or for whom a claim can be made?
      `the deceased was a minor at the date of his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deceased a minor at the date of his death?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I claim damages for bereavement` IS
    `s 21(2) the claim for damages for bereavement is for the benefit of the person` `which of these describes me` `I survive the deceased` `a claim can be made by or for a surviving spouse` `a claim can be made by or for a surviving child` `a claim can be made by or for a surviving parent` `a claim can be made by or for a person who treated the deceased as a child of the family` `the deceased was a minor at the date of his death`

@export What sum is awarded as damages for bereavement (s 21(4))?
GIVEN `the damages are awarded under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the damages awarded under section 21?
      `the sum the Minister has substituted, if any` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Minister has substituted another sum by order published in the Gazette, what is it, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What sum is awarded as damages for bereavement` IS
    `s 21(4) the sum to be awarded as damages for bereavement` `the damages are awarded under section 21` (IF `the sum the Minister has substituted, if any` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the sum the Minister has substituted, if any`)

@export Is this item taken into account in assessing the damages in an action under section 20 (s 22(1))?
GIVEN `the action is brought under section 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought under section 20?
      `the item` IS A `Item in assessing damages under section 22` @desc Is the item a sum under a contract of assurance or insurance, a sum under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953, a pension or gratuity paid as a result of the death, the remarriage of a widow, or another item?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this item taken into account in assessing the dependants' damages` IS
    `s 22(1) the item is taken into account in assessing the damages` `the action is brought under section 20` `the item`


§§ `Estates, rents and the survivorship of the dead (ss 24 to 30)`

@export Is the executor deemed a trustee of the undisposed residue for the person who would be entitled on an intestacy (s 24)?
GIVEN `the will appointed an executor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person by his will appoint a person to be his executor?
      `the property is residue not expressly disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property residue not expressly disposed of by the will?
      `the will shows the executor was intended to take the residue beneficially` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear by the will that the executor was intended to take the residue beneficially?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the executor a trustee of the residue for the person entitled on intestacy` IS
    `s 24 the executor is deemed to be a trustee for the person entitled in case of intestacy` `the will appointed an executor` `the property is residue not expressly disposed of` `the will shows the executor was intended to take the residue beneficially`

@export Can the devisee of mortgaged land require the mortgage debt to be paid out of the movable property or other land (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `the person died seised of or entitled to land that was charged by way of mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person die seised of or entitled to an estate or interest in immovable property that was at his death charged by way of mortgage?
      `I am the devisee to whom the land is devised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the devisee to whom the land is devised?
      `the person signified a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person by his will, deed or other document signify a contrary or other intention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the devisee make the estate pay off the mortgage` IS
    `s 26(1) the devisee is entitled to have the mortgage debt discharged out of the movable property or any other immovable property` `the person died seised of or entitled to land that was charged by way of mortgage` `I am the devisee to whom the land is devised` `the person signified a contrary intention`

@export Is a tenant who holds over chargeable, at my option as landlord, with double rent (s 28(4))?
GIVEN `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the tenant hold over after the determination of his tenancy?
      `the landlord opts for double the rent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the landlord opt for double the amount of the rent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my tenant who held over chargeable with double rent` IS
    `s 28(4) the tenant is chargeable with double the amount of his rent` `the tenant holds over after the determination of his tenancy` `the landlord opts for double the rent`

@export Does the duty arise for me, a subtenant, to give notice of the landlord's claim to my immediate landlord (s 28(5))?
GIVEN `an originating claim for recovery of the property has been served on me or I know of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an originating claim issued by a landlord against a tenant for the recovery of immovable property been served on you, or come to your knowledge?
      `I am a subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant?
      `I occupy the whole or part of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy the whole or any part of the premises sought to be recovered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I as a subtenant give notice of the landlord's claim` IS
    `s 28(5) the duty of the subtenant to give notice to his immediate landlord arises` `an originating claim for recovery of the property has been served on me or I know of it` `I am a subtenant of the claimant's immediate tenant` `I occupy the whole or part of the premises`

@export Have I, a subtenant, given my immediate landlord notice of the claim forthwith (s 28(5))?
GIVEN `the duty to give notice arises for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the duty to give notice arise for you (see the question just above)?
      `I have given notice to my immediate landlord forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of the originating claim to your immediate landlord forthwith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given my immediate landlord notice forthwith` IS
    `s 28(5) the subtenant has given notice to his immediate landlord forthwith` `the duty to give notice arises for me` `I have given notice to my immediate landlord forthwith`

@export Are two deaths, where it is uncertain who survived, presumed to have occurred in order of seniority (s 30)?
GIVEN `it is uncertain which of the persons survived the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did two or more persons die in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other or others?
      `the question affects the title to property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question one affecting the title to property?
      `the court has made an order to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order to the contrary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the death of two people presumed to have been in order of seniority` IS
    `s 30 the deaths are presumed to have occurred in order of seniority` `it is uncertain which of the persons survived the other` `the question affects the title to property` `the court has made an order to the contrary`


§§ `Settlements: accumulation, perpetuities, powers (ss 31 to 34)`

@export May the income of a settlement made before 15 December 2004 be accumulated for this period (s 31(2))?
GIVEN `the date the settlement or disposition was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the settlement or disposition made?
      `the period` IS A `Period of accumulation` @desc Which of the permitted periods fits the direction (the settlor's life; 21 years from the death; the minority of persons living at the death; the minority only of those who would be entitled; 21 years from the making; the minority of persons living at the making), or none of them?
      `the provision is for the payment of debts or the raising of portions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision one for payment of debts, or for raising portions for children or remoter issue (s 31(4))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `For how long may income be accumulated under an older settlement` IS
    `s 31(2) the income may be accumulated for the period` `the date the settlement or disposition was made` `the period` `the provision is for the payment of debts or the raising of portions`

-- The question takes no list of public holidays: a last day that is a Sunday moves to the next day (Interpretation Act s 50(b)), but a public holiday is not known.  Which day the term ends on is not set by the Act (fork F-S31-21).
@export On what date does a term of 21 years from the death of the grantor, settlor or testator end (s 31(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the grantor, settlor or testator die?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When does the 21-year term from the death end` IS
    `s 31(2)(b) the last day of the term of 21 years from the death` `the date of the death of the grantor settlor or testator` EMPTY

@export What is the perpetuity period for my settlement or disposition, in years (s 32)?
GIVEN `the rule against perpetuities applies to the settlement or disposition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the rule against perpetuities apply to the settlement or disposition?
      `the instrument refers to lives in being` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument refer to lives in being?
      `the period the instrument specifies, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What perpetuity period, in years, does the instrument specify? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the perpetuity period` IS
    `s 32 the perpetuity period in years` `the rule against perpetuities applies to the settlement or disposition` `the instrument refers to lives in being` (IF `the period the instrument specifies, in years` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the period the instrument specifies, in years`)

@export Can my disposition, which apart from section 34 would be invalid for remoteness, yet be treated as invalid (s 34(1))?
GIVEN `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid for remoteness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from section 34, would the disposition be invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities?
      `it has become certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the perpetuity period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it become certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the end of the perpetuity period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my disposition yet be treated as invalid for remoteness` IS
    `s 34(1) the disposition cannot yet be treated as invalid as infringing the rule against perpetuities` `apart from section 34 the disposition would be invalid for remoteness` `it has become certain that the vesting will occur, if at all, after the perpetuity period`


§§ `Minors who have attained 18, and medical advice (ss 35 to 37)`

@export Does my contract, made as a minor of 18 or over, have effect as if I were of full age (s 35)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I entered into the contract` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you enter into the contract?
      `another written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 35 itself (apart from subsections (4) and (5)) or another written law provide otherwise for this contract?
      `the kind of contract` IS A `Kind of contract by a minor who has attained 18` @desc What kind of contract is it (sale, purchase, mortgage, assignment or settlement of land; a lease of more than 3 years; a lease of 3 years or less; a sale or pledge of a beneficial interest under a trust; a settlement of legal proceedings or of a claim; extinguishing or varying a trust; or another kind)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my contract have effect as if I were of full age` IS
    `s 35 the contract has effect as if the minor were of full age` `my date of birth` `the date I entered into the contract` `another written law provides otherwise` `the kind of contract`

@export May I, aged 18 or over, bring or defend this legal proceeding in my own name without a litigation representative (s 36(1)(a))?
GIVEN `I have attained the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you attained the age of 18 years?
      `I am not otherwise under any legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you free of any other legal disability?
      `the proceeding is specified in the Schedule` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the proceeding or action one the Schedule specifies (a contract with full-age effect under section 35, acting as a company director or LLP manager, a bill of exchange, a registered business, or a registered limited partnership)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I conduct this legal proceeding in my own name` IS
    `s 36(1)(a) the minor may in his own name and without a litigation representative bring defend conduct or intervene in the proceeding or action as if he were of full age` `I have attained the age of 18 years` `I am not otherwise under any legal disability` (`what I say, as a fact` `the proceeding is specified in the Schedule`)

@export Did the healthcare professional meet the standard of care in giving me medical advice (s 37)?
GIVEN `the manner of acting is accepted by a respectable body of medical opinion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the way the healthcare professional acted, at the time the advice was given, accepted by a respectable body of medical opinion as reasonable professional practice in the circumstances?
      `that opinion requires the information a person in my circumstances would reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that opinion require the healthcare professional to have given the information that a person in your circumstances would reasonably require to make an informed decision?
      `that opinion requires the information material to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that opinion require the healthcare professional to have given the information that he knew or ought reasonably to know was material to you?
      `that opinion supports not giving information only where there is reasonable justification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that opinion support not giving any such information only where there is reasonable justification?
      `the body holding the opinion has directed its mind to the comparative risks and benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the body of healthcare professionals holding the opinion directed its mind to the comparative risks and benefits relating to the matter?
      `the opinion is internally consistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the opinion internally consistent?
      `the opinion does not contradict proven extrinsic facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the opinion avoid contradicting proven extrinsic facts relevant to the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the healthcare professional meet the standard of care for medical advice` IS
    `s 37 the healthcare professional meets the standard of care` `the manner of acting is accepted by a respectable body of medical opinion` `that opinion requires the information a person in my circumstances would reasonably require` `that opinion requires the information material to me` `that opinion supports not giving information only where there is reasonable justification` `the body holding the opinion has directed its mind to the comparative risks and benefits` `the opinion is internally consistent` `the opinion does not contradict proven extrinsic facts`

